Subject: [PATCH] wcn36xx: start firmware rate control at MCS0

The WCN3620 firmware table sends ENABLE_DYNAMIC_RA_START_RATE = 133
(0x85 = 0x80 | MCS5), i.e. the firmware opens every new TX rate-control
window at MCS5.  On this hardware (MSM8917 / ugglite) fast frames then die
in the air: measured 67-80 % loss, and the firmware ACK slot never fires
tx completion events.  Slow robust frames (1 Mbit/s beacons) pass, which
matches "aggressive start rate, no fallback in time".

Setting the value to 0 means "no forced start rate" (same value the
WCN3610-v3 series uses), letting firmware pick from its lowest retry set.

Measured on ugglite, same AP/station, 690 frames total: 0 % loss.
Stock module: 67-80 % loss.

TLV: WCN36XX_HAL_CFG_ENABLE_DYNAMIC_RA_START_RATE (id 210, hal.h).
Only the !RF_IRIS_WCN3680 table used by WCN3620 is touched; the
WCN3680-only table entry stays at its own value.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/wcn36xx/smd.c
@@ -79,7 +79,7 @@
 	WCN36XX_CFG_VAL(BTC_STATIC_LEN_LE_WLAN, 30000),
 	WCN36XX_CFG_VAL(MAX_ASSOC_LIMIT, 10),
 	WCN36XX_CFG_VAL(ENABLE_MCC_ADAPTIVE_SCHEDULER, 0),
-	WCN36XX_CFG_VAL(ENABLE_DYNAMIC_RA_START_RATE, 133), /* MCS 5 */
+	WCN36XX_CFG_VAL(ENABLE_DYNAMIC_RA_START_RATE, 0), /* MCS 5 */
 	WCN36XX_CFG_VAL(LINK_FAIL_TX_CNT, 1000),
 };
 
